17. Domestic Neglect is a person who neglects a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or because of an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide life, care, or maintenance to that person.
In addition, neglect also applies to every person who causes economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.
